{"items":[{"owner":{"account_id":137678,"reputation":1683,"user_id":8575,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/d9c550c19e95286c4eef4f79e4420c31?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"ogerard","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/8575/ogerard"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1548082409,"post_id":2784453,"comment_id":6353884,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"The book by Schwartz talks at length about how his family almost disappeared during WWII in France, and a lot of national and international politics starting in the 1930s up to the 1980s, from his initial trotskism up to his support for decolonization. His mathematical research, Bourbaki, the birth of distribution theory takes at most 1/5 of the book. There is also the french specific story about the math department of the Ecole Polytechnique."},{"owner":{"account_id":2638882,"reputation":52343,"user_id":72694,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":70,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/313420f3bb0aab434b130319e3f53bdc?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Mikhail Katz","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/72694/mikhail-katz"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526915217,"post_id":2788769,"comment_id":5753424,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Hi Alex, in my opinion Jeremy Gray&#39;s book is a profoundly flawed one and I wouldn&#39;t recommend it to anyone.  For one thing, he gobbles up hook, line, and sinker Mehrtens&#39; crazy thesis about Felix Klein being leader of a countermodern camp allegedly opposed to the modern camp led by Hilbert; see <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.02193\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">this 2018 forthcoming publication in Mat.Stud.</a> for details."},{"owner":{"account_id":2958470,"reputation":36475,"user_id":164025,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":64,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/275b37218440e1fd8dd350792e63d5c1?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Alex M.","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/164025/alex-m"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526824489,"post_id":2787618,"comment_id":5750624,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"The mathematics in it are light, indeed, but the history and cultural references within are not. I was going to post the same answer."},{"owner":{"account_id":2958470,"reputation":36475,"user_id":164025,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":64,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/275b37218440e1fd8dd350792e63d5c1?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Alex M.","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/164025/alex-m"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1526824397,"post_id":2784239,"comment_id":5750619,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This book is so poor, that I don&#39;t understand where it gets its fame from. Probably from being a pompous bunch of intellectual trivialities that make the average reader feel smart."},{"owner":{"account_id":1032304,"reputation":18976,"user_id":290240,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":91,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/pBHn1.png?s=256","display_name":"Sil","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/290240/sil"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1526726122,"post_id":2784138,"comment_id":5747941,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This book has similar one for applied math as well: <a href=\"https://rads.stackoverflow.com/amzn/click/com/0691150397\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">The Princeton Companion to Applied Mathematics</a>."},{"owner":{"account_id":2481725,"reputation":14016,"user_id":122782,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/bSFOB.png?s=256","display_name":"g.kov","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/122782/g-kov"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":510256,"reputation":411750,"user_id":622,"user_type":"moderator","accept_rate":87,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/8592b8e3b742e752b7b50d9ef1029931?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Asaf Karagila","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/622/asaf-karagila"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1526693112,"post_id":2786463,"comment_id":5747384,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Asaf Karagila: yes, I agree, Simon Singh is a good writer, and the books looks like well-suitable for recreational reading."},{"owner":{"account_id":510256,"reputation":411750,"user_id":622,"user_type":"moderator","accept_rate":87,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/8592b8e3b742e752b7b50d9ef1029931?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Asaf Karagila","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/622/asaf-karagila"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1526689828,"post_id":2786463,"comment_id":5747317,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"These books are far more interesting <i>before</i> you know mathematics, and if you like history, then before you know the actual history. Simon Singh is a good writer, but he took some... artistic freedoms with the history of things. Which might be a bit rattling to a mathematics professor."},{"owner":{"account_id":205170,"reputation":101,"user_id":87415,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/05f47f6982d68be135fa8caa7a798a74?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Robin Whittleton","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/87415/robin-whittleton"},"edited":false,"score":6,"creation_date":1526636682,"post_id":2784138,"comment_id":5745428,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"At 1000+ pages and over 2.5kg, you might want to consider buying an e-reader and an electronic copy for your sick friend."},{"owner":{"account_id":511397,"reputation":211810,"user_id":9003,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/AiFRy.jpg?s=256","display_name":"amWhy","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/9003/amwhy"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":473127,"reputation":294929,"user_id":14366,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":79,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/f76d986b54e90fa6c431160e9a0796cd?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"hmakholm left over Monica","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/14366/hmakholm-left-over-monica"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1526592164,"post_id":2783876,"comment_id":5744313,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Exactly, @HenningMakholm.  It&#39;s also a textbook used in undergraduate teacher education programs for elementary and secondary school teachers to-be."},{"owner":{"account_id":473127,"reputation":294929,"user_id":14366,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":79,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/f76d986b54e90fa6c431160e9a0796cd?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"hmakholm left over Monica","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/14366/hmakholm-left-over-monica"},"edited":false,"score":8,"creation_date":1526559452,"post_id":2783876,"comment_id":5743039,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This was the textbook of an undergraduate course I took decades ago. So I&#39;m not sure it passes the OP&#39;s ban on &quot;anything aimed at the undergraduate/postgraduate level&quot;."},{"owner":{"account_id":510256,"reputation":411750,"user_id":622,"user_type":"moderator","accept_rate":87,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/8592b8e3b742e752b7b50d9ef1029931?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Asaf Karagila","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/622/asaf-karagila"},"edited":false,"score":7,"creation_date":1526553924,"post_id":2784857,"comment_id":5742874,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Of course, there&#39;s no mention of the relation between the user posting this paper and the authors of the paper. But it&#39;s important to say it&#39;s an engaging read."},{"owner":{"account_id":2638882,"reputation":52343,"user_id":72694,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":70,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/313420f3bb0aab434b130319e3f53bdc?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Mikhail Katz","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/72694/mikhail-katz"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1526552855,"post_id":2783876,"comment_id":5742851,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"An explanation of the cultural reference can be found <a href=\"https://math.stackexchange.com/q/445166/72694\">here</a>."},{"owner":{"account_id":2575293,"reputation":5661,"user_id":186296,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":97,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/99c7f2d1368d561fb6f46cd009c729b8?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Klangen","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/186296/klangen"},"edited":false,"score":5,"creation_date":1526552390,"post_id":2784458,"comment_id":5742836,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I might be wrong here, but I find it quite improbable that a FRS has not yet read Littlewood&#39;s Miscellany..."},{"owner":{"account_id":3024795,"reputation":101,"user_id":94661,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2e60afb5fd938dcc5c4de0e897b374b2?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Crazy Yoghurt","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/94661/crazy-yoghurt"},"edited":false,"score":19,"creation_date":1526546498,"post_id":2784239,"comment_id":5742658,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I wouldn&#39;t recommend it for advanced reader. Hofstadter is as patronising as one can be."},{"owner":{"account_id":1046173,"reputation":101,"user_id":418702,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/dea1b533b826862b1123018117b11661?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Krazy Glew","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/418702/krazy-glew"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526518573,"post_id":2784021,"comment_id":5742064,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"...yet I recall stories from Newman all the time [fixed spelling]. I have long thought that there should be classes taught using Newman and similar material - it might inspire mathematical interest in students more literary than formulaic."},{"owner":{"account_id":1046173,"reputation":101,"user_id":418702,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/dea1b533b826862b1123018117b11661?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Krazy Glew","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/418702/krazy-glew"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526518214,"post_id":2784021,"comment_id":5742057,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I don’t know if Newman is advanced enough for an FRS, but I highly recommend it for kids in high school or advanced elementary. I remember rolling my eyes when my dad gave it me for Xmas - not because I wasn’t interested in math, but because it was so different from how math was taught in school - yet I recall stories from it all the times."},{"owner":{"account_id":4456944,"reputation":157,"user_id":370408,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/fc4b9562201cbda6603de8108e94dd08?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"CulDeVu","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/370408/culdevu"},"edited":false,"score":5,"creation_date":1526496234,"post_id":2783885,"comment_id":5741332,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Mathematics and Its History is the book we used in our undergraduate math history course, and it is certainly aimed towards undergraduates"},{"owner":{"account_id":510256,"reputation":411750,"user_id":622,"user_type":"moderator","accept_rate":87,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/8592b8e3b742e752b7b50d9ef1029931?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Asaf Karagila","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/622/asaf-karagila"},"edited":false,"score":132,"creation_date":1526493745,"post_id":2783876,"comment_id":5741218,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"History is written by the Victors, so that would be a very appropriate choice!"}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":254}